  "ingredients": [
    "16 ounce flat iron steak",
    "1/4 cup soy sauce",
    "2 teaspoon fresh garlic (chopped)",
    "1 teaspoon fresh ginger (peeled and grated)",
    "8 ounce broccoli (cut into small florets)",
    "1/4 cup avocado oil",
    "1/4 teaspoon xanthan gum",
    "1 teaspoon sesame oil",
    "1 teaspoon fish sauce"
  ],
  "instructions": [
    {
      "text": "Prep all ingredients.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/keto-beef-and-broccoli/#wprm-recipe-53445-step-0-0",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/Keto-low-carb-beef-and-broccoli-1.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Slice the flat iron steak into thin slices. Make sure to slice against the grain so that the beef is not chewy in the finished dish.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/keto-beef-and-broccoli/#wprm-recipe-53445-step-0-1",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/Keto-low-carb-beef-and-broccoli-2.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Combine the beef with the soy sauce, garlic, and ginger in a small tupperware or plastic bag. Let marinate for at least 30 minutes.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/keto-beef-and-broccoli/#wprm-recipe-53445-step-0-2",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/Keto-low-carb-beef-and-broccoli-4.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "When ready to cook, bring a pot of water to a boil. Blanch the broccoli for 2-3 minutes, then remove from water and drain thoroughly. Set aside.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/keto-beef-and-broccoli/#wprm-recipe-53445-step-0-3",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/Keto-low-carb-beef-and-broccoli-7.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Drain the marinade from the beef, reserving the marinade for later (this will be the stir-fry sauce).",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/keto-beef-and-broccoli/#wprm-recipe-53445-step-0-4",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/Keto-low-carb-beef-and-broccoli-5.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "In a pan over high heat, add the avocado oil. Once hot, add the beef and stir-fry for 2-3 minutes or until browned. Once browned, remove from the pan, leaving any remaining oil in the pan.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/keto-beef-and-broccoli/#wprm-recipe-53445-step-0-5",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/Keto-low-carb-beef-and-broccoli-8.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Add broccoli into the pan and cook for another 2-3 minutes or until broccoli is crisp but tender. Add the reserved marinade liquid and into the pan and cook for another 1-2 minutes. Once you add the marinade into the pan, sprinkle xanthan gum over the liquid and stir to help thicken.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/keto-beef-and-broccoli/#wprm-recipe-53445-step-0-6",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/Keto-low-carb-beef-and-broccoli-9.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Place the beef back into the pan along with the fish sauce and toasted sesame oil to warm through.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/keto-beef-and-broccoli/#wprm-recipe-53445-step-0-7",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/Keto-low-carb-beef-and-broccoli-11.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Once everything is hot, serve immediately.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/keto-beef-and-broccoli/#wprm-recipe-53445-step-0-8",
      "imageSource": null
    }
  ],
